here's something I want to ask you  should I interview more right-wingers  and when I say right-wingers it could be  Republican candidates or elected  officials  it could be conservative think-tank  people it could be the right-wing  extremists that I used to do much more  frequently like the Westboro Baptist  Church types or neo-nazis or whoever  else and the reason that this has come  up is that in the wake of my discussion  last week about attending politican this  political convention where political  conference where they have debates and  panels that might on some level be  interesting they might make for good  television but no real political issues  are going to be resolved the dialogue is  not going to be advanced by the types of  debates that by and large are happening  at politican so I went to the audience  and said what do you think is this  something that I should participate in  and in the wake of that a lot of people  emailed and they said you know I'm less  interested in political David but what I  would be interested in is you doing more  debates interviews debate style  interviews with people that are on the  right could be the far right could be  the less far right and I want to ask you  what you think about that because on the  one hand I don't subscribe to this idea  that dialogue merely for the sake of  dialogue is worth much if the dialogue  is happening in bad faith if the  dialogue is to people talking over each  other at the same time trying to score  political points without actually  discussing important issues so I don't  know we kind of go through phases where  we'll do more adversarial interviews and  then we'll kind of step back a little  bit from that they tend to do pretty  well in terms of audience interest and  audience size and feedback some people  like them more than others and I want to  sort of split the question up into two  one is are you interested in more  debates around policy with right-wingers  a libertarian about libertarian ideas or  someone who believes that low taxes on  the rich are good for the  sort of there's that and then the  question there is is it the same old  talking points all the time is there  anything new to learn or or achieve from  that that would be question one question  two is the other side of it which is  what about the more colorful extremists  do we want do you want me doing more  interviews with the homophobes the white  nationalists the religious ideologues  those types and does do we learn  anything from them it's fun to do it  it's fun to prepare for it they tend to  do well there's sort of like a shock  value but a lot of it devolves into  nonsense they very often won't answer  direct questions and and actually even  the right-wingers that I do sometimes  will debate on policy will use the  standard distraction tactics where I try  to really drill down on issues they  respond with non answers and  distractions like we all know the  techniques so is there something to be  gained what are the adversarial type  interviews that you want me to do what  are the ones that are maybe less  interesting to you and there's two views  on this often one is yes it's worth  getting people on and challenging their  ideas not necessarily because you're  going to change their mind but because  people will see it and it's the audience  whose mind may be changed it doesn't  really matter if you change one  libertarian economist mind but if  several thousand or tens of thousands of  people see that particular clip that's  where you might change the minds of a  hundred people or of a thousand people  or five hundred or who knows what the  number is the other side would be it's  just not worth a day but bring on people  who are coming up with innovative ideas  that we can get behind people on the  Left progressives and Social Democrats  and others let's talk to them and just  put good ideas out there I want to hear  from you you can let me know by using  the contact form at david pakman.com you  can tweet me at Deep hackman or tweet  the show at David Pakman show you can go  on our Facebook page facebook.com slash  David Pakman show you can even let me  know on Instagram if you  David Pakman on Instagram or at david  pakman show on instagram and by the way  if you're not following at david pakman  show on instagram please do lots of  interesting behind-the-scenes pictures  memes you can either even see what my  sort of temporary studio here in paris  france has looked like we've got a great  behind-the-scenes picture of the studio  up on the show instagram account at  david pakman show  so we'll take a quick break next we will  deal with the pseudoscience of detoxes  and cleanses in today's pseudo science  mini-series episode and then much much  more coming up including your voicemail  more news and eventually the bonus show
 

